A||N||5||RedOktober||whats a good price for a turbo kit?||||5||
Z||000000||RedOktober||09-21-2000||09:57 PM||||It seems that there are a few of Fiero fans out there that are always talking about installing a Turbo onto your cars. My question to everbody thats wants one is "How much would be a good price for a turbo kit?"<BR>and How complete do you guys want it? ie: Basic or Deluxe?<P>Any response and suggestions would be appreciated.<P>------------------<BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater)||||reg||5
Z||000001||Xtreme Fiero's||09-21-2000||11:23 PM||||<P>   I think $100-$150 per pound of boost would be a great price. I think i'm dreaming.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||RedOktober||09-22-2000||01:24 AM||||maybe I should restate this. <BR>I know design1 has a turbo kit for about $3000 and IRM is not too off that mark. Each of those are good kits. But some feel that is a bit much for the average guy or gal. <BR>So how much would you pay for a reliable 200- 275hp, (depending on your set up) and without having to get the bottle refilled after 5-10 hit of NOS.||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||09-22-2000||08:28 AM||||3 grand is a good price... we sell turbo kits for other cars.. not including piping and ECU mods that sell for more than that. or if your pretty good at fabrication check out <A HREF="http://www.turboneticsinc.com" TARGET=_blank>www.turboneticsinc.com</A>  and order your own T-04S and build your own... in doing that you'll get the look you want AND you'll be able to have an intercooler with out redesigning the entire kit. not sure about Xtremes money numbers.. with his numbers you'll have 20psi for 3k.. uum you'll need that much in the motor just to handle 1.5bar. I wish it was that cheap... i'd be runnin 20psi!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> your gunna have issues with much over 10psi and you'll have $1500 in parts (no tubing, ignition, fuel) Turbo $1000-$1500, blow off valve $250, external wastegate $300, MSD 6BTM $320, and custom tubing $250-300, Silicon couplings $50-60, injectors $350, fuel pump $150, VOrtech Sfmu $250, and a host of other stuff...<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 09-22-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||09-22-2000||04:53 PM||||I would pay $2000 if thats possible.||||reg||1
Z||000005||contra||09-23-2000||10:39 AM||||i want a turbo kit so bad<BR>but after a talk with some fiero experts it looks like it'd be more money and hassle than it's worth...for me anyways.<P>i think i'm just going to spend a good $700 or so bucks on a nitro system, nothing too powerfull, but something to give a good kick if i ever need it, or just for fun  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>if my engine ever dies...i'll just attempt to swap in a carb v8 lol!<BR>||||reg||1
